<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the generated macOS Info.plist by the Tauri bundler.

  Both keys are mandatory, not advisory: macOS terminates an app that asks
  for either permission without a purpose string in its bundle, so leaving
  one out does not degrade the feature, it kills the process.

  The screen-recording string carries the explanation for what would
  otherwise look like an overreach — a meeting-notes app asking to record
  the screen. ScreenCaptureKit is the only supported way to capture system
  audio on macOS (ADR-0024), and no video is ever requested or read.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Resumeira records your microphone so it can transcribe your side of the meeting. The audio stays on this Mac unless you configure a transcription service yourself.</string>

    <key>NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Resumeira records the audio your Mac plays — the other people in the meeting. macOS provides that only through screen recording; Resumeira never receives, stores or sends any image of your screen.</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
